# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities. What makes the route interesting is a single idea, taken from the *flow set* framework of Gandon et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the work that also motivated the [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") in this package:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini membina litar untuk **dinamik masa model Fermi-Hubbard satu dimensi**, daripada menulis Hamiltonian hingga menyemak ketumpatan tapak yang telah berevolusi. Apa yang menjadikan laluan ini menarik ialah satu idea, yang diambil daripada rangka kerja *set aliran* oleh Gandon et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), kerja yang turut mendorong [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") dalam pakej ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Instead of grouping Hamiltonian terms *after* the fermion-to-qubit mapping, group them *before* it, into **flow sets**, one-dimensional subsets of the directed fermionic interaction graph whose transfer operators mutually commute.\n"
msgstr "> Daripada mengumpulkan sebutan Hamiltonian *selepas* pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit, kumpulkan *sebelum* pemetaan itu, ke dalam **set aliran**, subset satu dimensi bagi graf interaksi fermion berarah yang operator pindahannya saling kalis tukar tertib.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That choice drives everything below. It calls for the following:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan itu mendorong segala-galanya di bawah. Ia memerlukan yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom fermion-to-qubit encoding** tailored to the flow sets, which here spends one **ancilla qubit** so the qubit count associated with the implementation of a given Hamiltonian term no longer grows with the number of fermionic modes (as is the case for Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"
msgstr "**Pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit tersuai** yang disesuaikan dengan set aliran, yang di sini menggunakan satu **qubit bantu** supaya bilangan qubit yang dikaitkan dengan pelaksanaan sebutan Hamiltonian tertentu tidak lagi meningkat mengikut bilangan mod fermion (seperti yang berlaku bagi Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom synthesis** that exploits the commutativity within each set. The payoff is a circuit whose two-qubit depth is **constant in the system size**, against the linear growth of a JW-based term-by-term Trotterization.\n"
msgstr "**Sintesis tersuai** yang memanfaatkan kekalisan tukar tertib dalam setiap set. Faedahnya ialah litar yang kedalaman dua-qubitnya **malar terhadap saiz sistem**, berbanding pertumbuhan linear Trotterisasi sebutan demi sebutan berasaskan JW.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The machinery that gets an encoding of your own into the transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) carries over to any model.\n"
msgstr "Jentera yang memasukkan pengekodan anda sendiri ke dalam transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) boleh digunakan pada mana-mana model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout, and the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the general recipe for writing a custom mapper.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Lihat juga\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [Panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) untuk peringkat transpiler yang dirujuk sepanjang panduan ini, dan [panduan pemeta](mappers#mappers-explanation) untuk resipi umum menulis pemeta tersuai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transfer operators and flow sets {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"
msgstr "Operator pindahan dan set aliran {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") is built from vertex operators $V_j$ and transfer operators $T_{jk}$. In terms of fermionic creation and annihilation operators,\n"
msgstr "[`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") dibina daripada operator bucu $V_j$ dan operator pindahan $T_{jk}$. Dari segi operator penciptaan dan pemusnahan fermion,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so $V_j$ measures the occupation of mode $j$ (it is $+1$ when empty and $-1$ when filled), while $T_{jk}$ transfers a fermion along the *directed* edge $j \\to k$. Note that the two indices of $T_{jk}$ are *not* interchangeable. The first index carries the minus combination and the second carries the plus, which is what makes $T_{jk}$ distinct from $T_{kj}$ and gives the edge its orientation.\n"
msgstr "jadi $V_j$ mengukur penghunian mod $j$ (ia $+1$ apabila kosong dan $-1$ apabila terisi), manakala $T_{jk}$ memindahkan fermion sepanjang tepi *berarah* $j \\to k$. Perhatikan bahawa dua indeks $T_{jk}$ *tidak* boleh ditukar ganti. Indeks pertama membawa gabungan tolak dan indeks kedua membawa tambah, itulah yang menjadikan $T_{jk}$ berbeza daripada $T_{kj}$ dan memberi tepi itu orientasinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These satisfy *mixed* commutation relations. Two transfer operators acting on **disjoint** sites commute trivially, since each is an *even* product of fermionic operators. The interesting case is a shared site. There, the two **commute** if the arrows *flow* through that site (one arrives, one leaves) and **anticommute** if they *clash* (both arrive, or both leave).\n"
msgstr "Ini memenuhi hubungan kalis tukar tertib *campuran*. Dua operator pindahan yang bertindak pada tapak **terpisah** adalah kalis tukar tertib secara remeh, kerana setiap satu ialah hasil darab *genap* bagi operator fermion. Kes yang menarik ialah tapak yang dikongsi. Di situ, kedua-duanya **kalis tukar tertib** jika anak panah *mengalir* melalui tapak itu (satu tiba, satu pergi) dan **antikalis tukar tertib** jika ia *berlanggar* (kedua-duanya tiba, atau kedua-duanya pergi).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rule is easiest to see on a picture. Drawing the vertices as nodes and each $T_{jk}$ as an arrow from $j$ to $k$ gives the *directed* interaction graph, here for the four-site chain used throughout this guide, which carries both orientations of every bond:\n"
msgstr "Peraturan ini paling mudah dilihat pada gambar. Melukis bucu sebagai nod dan setiap $T_{jk}$ sebagai anak panah daripada $j$ ke $k$ memberikan graf interaksi *berarah*, di sini untuk rantai empat tapak yang digunakan sepanjang panduan ini, yang membawa kedua-dua orientasi bagi setiap ikatan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace the rule on the figure. Look at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{2,3}$, for example. One arrow *arrives* at site 2 and the other *leaves* it, so the fermion flows straight through and the two operators commute. Look instead at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{3,2}$. Both arrows *point into* site 2. They clash, and those two anticommute.\n"
msgstr "Jejaki peraturan pada rajah. Lihat $T_{1,2}$ dan $T_{2,3}$, sebagai contoh. Satu anak panah *tiba* di tapak 2 dan satu lagi *meninggalkannya*, jadi fermion mengalir terus melaluinya dan kedua-dua operator kalis tukar tertib. Sebaliknya lihat $T_{1,2}$ dan $T_{3,2}$. Kedua-dua anak panah *menuju ke* tapak 2. Ia berlanggar, dan kedua-duanya antikalis tukar tertib.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is what makes flow sets possible. Pick a set of arrows forming a directed path and every pair either meets head-to-tail or does not meet at all, so the whole set commutes, even though the individual operators overlap on shared sites. Evolving under a single flow set therefore incurs **no Trotter error**, and as [step 7](#flowsets-synthesis) shows, it can also be done at constant circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Inilah yang membolehkan set aliran. Pilih set anak panah yang membentuk laluan berarah dan setiap pasangan sama ada bertemu kepala-ke-ekor atau tidak bertemu langsung, jadi seluruh set kalis tukar tertib, walaupun operator individu bertindih pada tapak yang dikongsi. Berevolusi di bawah satu set aliran oleh itu tidak menanggung **ralat Trotter**, dan seperti ditunjukkan oleh [langkah 7](#flowsets-synthesis), ia juga boleh dilakukan pada kedalaman litar malar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian Fermi-Hubbard {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D Fermi-Hubbard model on $L$ sites (spinless, open boundaries) is\n"
msgstr "Model Fermi-Hubbard 1D pada $L$ tapak (tanpa spin, sempadan terbuka) ialah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following Eq. (9) of Ref. <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the hopping term is $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. The interaction is diagonal, so it is expressed through vertex operators using $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"
msgstr "Mengikut Pers. (9) Rujukan <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), sebutan lompatan ialah $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. Interaksi bersifat pepenjuru, jadi ia dinyatakan melalui operator bucu menggunakan $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both pieces are built directly as a [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Note that $V_j$ is stored as the diagonal entry `(j, j)`:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua bahagian dibina terus sebagai [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Perhatikan bahawa $V_j$ disimpan sebagai entri pepenjuru `(j, j)`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interior sites pick up a coefficient of $-1$ on $V_j$ because they appear in two bonds, whereas the boundary sites only appear in one. Every term listed here appears in the graph drawn above. The `T(j,k)` terms are its arrows, and the `V(j)` terms its nodes.\n"
msgstr "Tapak dalaman mendapat pekali $-1$ pada $V_j$ kerana ia muncul dalam dua ikatan, manakala tapak sempadan hanya muncul dalam satu. Setiap sebutan yang disenaraikan di sini muncul dalam graf yang dilukis di atas. Sebutan `T(j,k)` ialah anak panahnya, dan sebutan `V(j)` ialah nodnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"partition-into-flow-sets\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Partition into flow sets {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"
msgstr "2. Bahagikan kepada set aliran {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, label each term with the flow set it belongs to. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute exists for this purpose. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per group ([step 6](#flowsets-transpile) puts this to work), so the grouping decided here at the *fermionic* level survives into the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, labelkan setiap sebutan dengan set aliran yang dimilikinya. Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") wujud untuk tujuan ini. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ke atas operator yang dikumpulkan terurai kepada satu [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") bagi setiap kumpulan ([langkah 6](#flowsets-transpile) menggunakannya), jadi pengumpulan yang diputuskan di sini pada aras *fermion* kekal dalam litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the 1D chain, the two hopping flow sets are the east-oriented arrows ($T_{j,j+1}$) and the west-oriented arrows ($T_{j+1,j}$). The diagonal interaction terms commute with everything diagonal and form a third group:\n"
msgstr "Bagi rantai 1D, dua set aliran lompatan ialah anak panah berorientasi timur ($T_{j,j+1}$) dan anak panah berorientasi barat ($T_{j+1,j}$). Sebutan interaksi pepenjuru kalis tukar tertib dengan segala yang pepenjuru dan membentuk kumpulan ketiga:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups 0 and 1 are the two flow sets. Each set is a directed path along the chain, so by the flow property all terms within a group commute.\n"
msgstr "Kumpulan 0 dan 1 ialah dua set aliran. Setiap set ialah laluan berarah sepanjang rantai, jadi mengikut sifat aliran semua sebutan dalam satu kumpulan kalis tukar tertib.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group also has to be Hermitian on its own, since a product formula exponentiates the groups separately and only a Hermitian factor has a unitary evolution. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") confirms it:\n"
msgstr "Setiap kumpulan juga mesti Hermitian dengan sendirinya, kerana formula hasil darab mengeksponenkan kumpulan secara berasingan dan hanya faktor Hermitian mempunyai evolusi unitari. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") mengesahkannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is worth pausing on, because the two hopping groups are *one-directional*: group 0 holds only east-oriented terms and group 1 only west-oriented ones. Splitting a Hamiltonian that way would normally break Hermiticity, since $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ needs its conjugate partner $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ alongside it. A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") avoids the problem because $T_{jk}$ is *already* Hermitian on its own. It is a product of two Majorana operators (see its definition in step 1), not a bare $a^\\dagger_j a_k$, so its Jordan-Wigner image carries a real coefficient rather than an imaginary one. Choosing this operator representation is therefore what makes a one-directional flow set a legitimate Trotter factor at all.\n"
msgstr "Itu patut diberi perhatian, kerana dua kumpulan lompatan itu *sehala*: kumpulan 0 hanya mengandungi sebutan berorientasi timur dan kumpulan 1 hanya yang berorientasi barat. Memisahkan Hamiltonian dengan cara itu biasanya akan memecahkan sifat Hermitian, kerana $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ memerlukan pasangan konjugatnya $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ bersama-samanya. [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") mengelakkan masalah ini kerana $T_{jk}$ *sudah* Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Ia ialah hasil darab dua operator Majorana (lihat takrifnya dalam langkah 1), bukan $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ semata-mata, jadi imej Jordan-Wigner-nya membawa pekali nyata dan bukan khayal. Memilih perwakilan operator ini oleh itu menjadikan set aliran sehala sebagai faktor Trotter yang sah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The east/west labels used throughout this guide are **geometric**, with the chain drawn left to right and mode indices increasing in that direction; $T_{j,j+1}$ points east and $T_{j+1,j}$ points west. Ref.   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) is internally inconsistent on this naming (its prose and its figures disagree) so this guide deliberately does *not* follow the prose, and instead keeps the labels from the picture. When cross-reading with the paper, match the flow sets by their Pauli weights (1 and 3 below), not by the compass words.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Label timur/barat yang digunakan sepanjang panduan ini bersifat **geometri**, dengan rantai dilukis dari kiri ke kanan dan indeks mod meningkat ke arah itu; $T_{j,j+1}$ menghala ke timur dan $T_{j+1,j}$ menghala ke barat. Rujukan   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) tidak konsisten secara dalaman tentang penamaan ini (prosa dan rajahnya tidak sepadan) jadi panduan ini sengaja *tidak* mengikut prosa, sebaliknya mengekalkan label daripada gambar. Apabila merujuk silang dengan kertas itu, padankan set aliran mengikut pemberat Pauli (1 dan 3 di bawah), bukan mengikut perkataan arah mata angin.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"write-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Write the custom encoding {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Tulis pengekodan tersuai {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Section IV B of Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) classifies the forms that a local fermion-to-qubit encoding can take when restricted to a flow set. Plain Jordan-Wigner uses $N_q = N_f$ qubits and maps every hopping term to a weight-2 Pauli. The classification shows that **spending extra qubits buys structure** in the encoded operators.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian IV B Rujukan <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) mengelaskan bentuk yang boleh diambil oleh pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit setempat apabila terhad kepada satu set aliran. Jordan-Wigner biasa menggunakan $N_q = N_f$ qubit dan memetakan setiap sebutan lompatan kepada Pauli berpemberat 2. Pengelasan itu menunjukkan bahawa **membelanjakan qubit tambahan membeli struktur** dalam operator yang dikodkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding implemented here is the parity-delocalized construction of Appendix B 2 (equations B4 and B5), which uses one **ancilla qubit**, so $N_q = N_f + 1$. The fermionic parity is delocalized across a pair of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan yang dilaksanakan di sini ialah binaan penyetempatan-nyah pariti dalam Lampiran B 2 (persamaan B4 dan B5), yang menggunakan satu **qubit bantu**, jadi $N_q = N_f + 1$. Pariti fermion dinyahsetempatkan merentas sepasang qubit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The index $j+2$ in the last expression forces the extra qubit. The chain’s final bond has $j = N_f - 2$, so its $Z_{j+2}$ lands on qubit $N_f$, one past the last fermionic mode $N_f - 1$. That trailing qubit is the ancilla, and it is why $N_q = N_f + 1$ rather than $N_f$. The same reach shows up in $V_j$, whose $Z_{j+1}$ is on the ancilla for $j = N_f - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Indeks $j+2$ dalam ungkapan terakhir memaksa qubit tambahan. Ikatan terakhir rantai mempunyai $j = N_f - 2$, jadi $Z_{j+2}$-nya jatuh pada qubit $N_f$, satu melepasi mod fermion terakhir $N_f - 1$. Qubit hujung itu ialah qubit bantu, dan itulah sebabnya $N_q = N_f + 1$ dan bukan $N_f$. Jangkauan yang sama muncul dalam $V_j$, yang $Z_{j+1}$-nya berada pada qubit bantu untuk $j = N_f - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is visible immediately; one whole flow set is mapped to a sum of weight-1 Paulis.\n"
msgstr "Faedahnya kelihatan serta-merta; satu set aliran penuh dipetakan kepada hasil tambah Pauli berpemberat 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ prefactors are fixed by the normalization $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, and the relative minus sign between the two orientations is fixed by the product identity $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, which the Paulis above satisfy. Getting either wrong yields an operator that obeys the commutation relations but no longer represents the same Hamiltonian, so you should verify the encoding numerically, as shown in [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Pemfaktor $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ ditetapkan oleh normalisasi $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, dan tanda tolak relatif antara dua orientasi ditetapkan oleh identiti hasil darab $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, yang dipenuhi oleh Pauli di atas. Tersalah salah satunya menghasilkan operator yang mematuhi hubungan kalis tukar tertib tetapi tidak lagi mewakili Hamiltonian yang sama, jadi anda harus mengesahkan pengekodan secara berangka, seperti ditunjukkan dalam [langkah 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing the encoding means writing a function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") handles the iteration over terms and their composition:\n"
msgstr "Menulis pengekodan bermaksud menulis fungsi yang memetakan satu operator pindahan teritlak kepada rentetan Pauli; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") mengendalikan lelaran ke atas sebutan dan gubahannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") expects the signature `(operator, num_qubits)`, and the return type must be a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which makes the function directly usable as a transpiler plugin. See [step 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") menjangkakan tandatangan `(operator, num_qubits)`, dan jenis pulangan mestilah [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), yang menjadikan fungsi itu boleh digunakan terus sebagai pemalam transpiler. Lihat [langkah 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying it to the Hamiltonian from step 1 gives the encoded operator on $N_f + 1 = 5$ qubits:\n"
msgstr "Menggunakannya pada Hamiltonian daripada langkah 1 memberikan operator terkod pada $N_f + 1 = 5$ qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are 14 terms, in three shapes: the hopping has become `X` and `ZXZ`, the interaction `ZZ`, and the leading `[]` is the identity, contributing only a global phase. Note that the `ZZ` terms reach nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors; $V_jV_{j+1}$ spans qubits $j$ through $j+2$, which is the cost of delocalizing the parity.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat 14 sebutan, dalam tiga bentuk: lompatan telah menjadi `X` dan `ZXZ`, interaksi `ZZ`, dan `[]` di awal ialah identiti, yang hanya menyumbang fasa global. Perhatikan bahawa sebutan `ZZ` mencapai jiran terdekat *dan* jiran kedua terdekat; $V_jV_{j+1}$ merentangi qubit $j$ hingga $j+2$, iaitu kos penyahsetempatan pariti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grouping by flow set exposes the asymmetry the construction buys. List the Pauli weights present in each group:\n"
msgstr "Pengumpulan mengikut set aliran mendedahkan ketaksimetrian yang dibeli oleh binaan ini. Senaraikan pemberat Pauli yang terdapat dalam setiap kumpulan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The east-oriented flow set (group 0) consists **entirely of weight-1 Paulis**. Its time evolution is therefore a layer of single-qubit rotations and needs *no entangling gates*, whereas under Jordan-Wigner every hopping term is weight-2 and requires them. This is the space-time trade-off of Ref. <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) in its simplest form: one extra qubit converts half of the hopping Hamiltonian into single-qubit rotations.\n"
msgstr "Set aliran berorientasi timur (kumpulan 0) terdiri **sepenuhnya daripada Pauli berpemberat 1**. Evolusi masanya oleh itu ialah satu lapisan putaran qubit tunggal dan *tidak memerlukan gate berbelit*, manakala di bawah Jordan-Wigner setiap sebutan lompatan berpemberat 2 dan memerlukannya. Inilah pertukaran ruang-masa Rujukan <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) dalam bentuk paling ringkas: satu qubit tambahan menukarkan separuh Hamiltonian lompatan kepada putaran qubit tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The west-oriented flow set (group 1) pays for it at weight three, and the interaction (group 2) sits at weight two, where the weight-zero entry is the identity. None of this is yet a *circuit* claim; what a synthesis makes of these weights is the subject of steps 6 and 7.\n"
msgstr "Set aliran berorientasi barat (kumpulan 1) membayarnya pada pemberat tiga, dan interaksi (kumpulan 2) berada pada pemberat dua, dengan entri pemberat sifar ialah identiti. Tiada satu pun ini lagi dakwaan tentang *litar*; apa yang dihasilkan oleh sintesis daripada pemberat ini ialah subjek langkah 6 dan 7.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Verify the encoding {#4-verify-the-encoding}"
msgstr "4. Sahkan pengekodan {#4-verify-the-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A custom encoding is only useful if it is *faithful*, and a hand-written one should be checked. Because this encoding uses $N_f + 1$ qubits, the qubit Hilbert space is twice as large as the fermionic one, so the encoded Hamiltonian cannot equal the Jordan-Wigner one term by term. The two are related by an isometry instead.\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan tersuai hanya berguna jika ia *setia*, dan yang ditulis dengan tangan harus disemak. Oleh sebab pengekodan ini menggunakan $N_f + 1$ qubit, ruang Hilbert qubit adalah dua kali ganda lebih besar daripada ruang fermion, jadi Hamiltonian terkod tidak boleh sama dengan Hamiltonian Jordan-Wigner sebutan demi sebutan. Kedua-duanya dikaitkan oleh isometri sebaliknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Where the isometry comes from:** Under Jordan-Wigner a basis state is the occupation string; qubit $j$ holds $n_j$. This encoding instead stores *cumulative parities*. Define\n"
msgstr "**Dari mana isometri datang:** Di bawah Jordan-Wigner, keadaan asas ialah rentetan penghunian; qubit $j$ memegang $n_j$. Pengekodan ini sebaliknya menyimpan *pariti longgokan*. Takrifkan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so bit $b_{j+1}$ records the parity of all occupations up to and including site $j$. There are $N_f + 1$ such bits for $N_f$ occupations, which is where the ancilla comes from. The occupation is recovered as the *difference* between neighboring bits, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. An occupied site therefore shows up as a **domain wall** between two adjacent bits, which is why this is called a domain-wall (or Kramers-Wannier) encoding. That is also why $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: the product of two neighboring $Z$s reads off that difference.\n"
msgstr "jadi bit $b_{j+1}$ merekodkan pariti semua penghunian sehingga dan termasuk tapak $j$. Terdapat $N_f + 1$ bit sedemikian bagi $N_f$ penghunian, dari situlah qubit bantu datang. Penghunian dipulihkan sebagai *perbezaan* antara bit berjiran, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. Tapak yang dihuni oleh itu muncul sebagai **dinding domain** antara dua bit bersebelahan, sebab itu ia dipanggil pengekodan dinding domain (atau Kramers-Wannier). Itu juga sebabnya $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: hasil darab dua $Z$ berjiran membaca perbezaan itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing this map out for a few states makes the structure concrete (note that $b_0 = 0$ is fixed, so only half of the $2^{N_f+1}$ qubit states are in the image, and hence an isometry rather than a unitary):\n"
msgstr "Menulis peta ini untuk beberapa keadaan menjadikan strukturnya jelas (perhatikan bahawa $b_0 = 0$ ditetapkan, jadi hanya separuh daripada keadaan qubit $2^{N_f+1}$ berada dalam imej, dan oleh itu ia isometri dan bukan uniter):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single fermion on site 0 flips every cumulative parity above it, which is the delocalization at work. Collecting these columns into a matrix gives the isometry $W$, and the encoding is faithful when it *intertwines* the two Hamiltonians:\n"
msgstr "Satu fermion pada tapak 0 membalikkan setiap pariti kumulatif di atasnya, dan inilah penyahsetempatan yang berlaku. Mengumpulkan lajur-lajur ini ke dalam matriks menghasilkan isometri $W$, dan pengekodan itu setia apabila ia *menjalin* kedua-dua Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, mapping a fermionic state into the qubit space and then evolving it there must give the same result as evolving it in the fermionic space first and mapping afterward.\n"
msgstr "Iaitu, memetakan keadaan fermion ke dalam ruang qubit dan kemudian mengembangkannya di sana mesti memberikan keputusan yang sama seperti mengembangkannya dahulu dalam ruang fermion dan memetakannya selepas itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The intertwining relation holds exactly, and separately for each flow set. That second, stronger statement is what later steps rely on: a product formula evolves the groups one at a time, and a product of intertwined factors is itself intertwined, so any *approximation* built from these groups agrees between the two encodings even though the encodings differ. As a corollary, the spectra must agree, with every Jordan-Wigner eigenvalue appearing twice in the larger space, once for each value of the unconstrained global parity:\n"
msgstr "Hubungan penjalinan ini berlaku dengan tepat, dan secara berasingan bagi setiap set aliran. Kenyataan kedua yang lebih kuat itulah yang bergantung padanya langkah-langkah seterusnya: formula hasil darab mengembangkan kumpulan satu demi satu, dan hasil darab faktor yang terjalin itu sendiri terjalin, jadi sebarang *penghampiran* yang dibina daripada kumpulan ini adalah sepadan antara kedua-dua pengekodan walaupun pengekodan itu berbeza. Sebagai akibatnya, spektrum mesti sepadan, dengan setiap nilai eigen Jordan-Wigner muncul dua kali dalam ruang yang lebih besar, sekali bagi setiap nilai pariti global yang tidak dikekang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-build\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Build the fermionic circuit {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "5. Bina litar fermion {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before involving any qubits, the dynamics are expressed on the *fermionic* level. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") acts on fermionic modes rather than qubits, and an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over the Hamiltonian is the whole circuit:\n"
msgstr "Sebelum melibatkan sebarang qubit, dinamik dinyatakan pada peringkat *fermion*. [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") bertindak ke atas mod fermion dan bukan qubit, dan gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ke atas Hamiltonian ialah keseluruhan litar:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one opaque box over all four modes, and the interesting part is what it decomposes into. The `synthesis` argument says how: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the first-order product formula, which splits the operator by its [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") and evolves each group in turn. So the flow-set partitioning from step 2 *is* the Trotterization, and a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) performs it, giving **one** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **per flow set** in group order: east, west, then the diagonal interaction, carrying 3, 3, and 8 terms respectively.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat satu kotak legap merentasi keempat-empat mod, dan bahagian yang menarik ialah apa yang diuraikannya. Argumen `synthesis` menyatakan caranya: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ialah formula hasil darab peringkat pertama, yang memecahkan operator mengikut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") dan mengembangkan setiap kumpulan secara bergilir. Jadi pembahagian set aliran daripada langkah 2 *ialah* penghampiran Trotter, dan satu [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) melaksanakannya, menghasilkan **satu** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **bagi setiap set aliran** mengikut tertib kumpulan: timur, barat, kemudian interaksi pepenjuru, masing-masing membawa 3, 3, dan 8 sebutan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this happens entirely in fermionic space: no qubit has been mentioned yet, and the approximation is already made. The number of Trotter steps therefore belongs here too, as [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), which divides the time and repeats the whole sweep:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa ini berlaku sepenuhnya dalam ruang fermion: tiada qubit yang disebut lagi, dan penghampiran sudah pun dibuat. Oleh itu bilangan langkah Trotter juga tergolong di sini, sebagai [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), yang membahagikan masa dan mengulang keseluruhan sapuan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nine gates: the three flow sets, cycled through three times at a third of the time each. That cycling is what makes it a Trotterization rather than a re-slicing of one group. Repeating a *single* group would achieve nothing, since consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` is just `A(t)`. A formula that reads the groups can interleave them; one applied after the mapping cannot, because the grouping is gone by then.\n"
msgstr "Sembilan gate: tiga set aliran, dikitar tiga kali pada sepertiga masa setiap satu. Kitaran itulah yang menjadikannya penghampiran Trotter dan bukan sekadar pembahagian semula satu kumpulan. Mengulang satu kumpulan *tunggal* tidak mencapai apa-apa, kerana eksponen berturut-turut bagi operator yang sama saling kalis tukar tertib, jadi `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` hanyalah `A(t)`. Formula yang membaca kumpulan boleh menyisipkannya; formula yang dikenakan selepas pemetaan tidak boleh, kerana pengelompokan sudah hilang pada ketika itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the step that makes the grouping matter. Each emitted gate is mapped and synthesized independently, so everything downstream acts on the partitioning decided at the fermionic level. Skipping the decomposition hands the whole operator to the next stage instead, and the grouping is ignored.\n"
msgstr "Inilah langkah yang menjadikan pengelompokan penting. Setiap gate yang dikeluarkan dipetakan dan disintesis secara bebas, jadi segala-galanya selepas ini bertindak berdasarkan pembahagian yang diputuskan pada peringkat fermion. Melangkau penguraian menyerahkan keseluruhan operator kepada peringkat seterusnya, dan pengelompokan diabaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Transpile with the custom encoding {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "6. Transpile dengan pengekodan tersuai {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is now ready to be used by the transpiler. Two more pieces are needed:\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan kini sedia digunakan oleh transpiler. Dua komponen lagi diperlukan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A layout.** The default [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") assumes one qubit per mode, which is wrong in this situation. [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") associates the fermionic register with a [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) of a different size, which is how ancilla qubits enter the pipeline.\n"
msgstr "**Susun atur.** [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") lalai mengandaikan satu qubit bagi setiap mod, yang salah dalam keadaan ini. [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") mengaitkan daftar fermion dengan [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) yang bersaiz berbeza, dan beginilah qubit ancilla memasuki saluran paip.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A synthesis plugin.** [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes the mapper function directly, maps the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate’s Hamiltonian with it, and emits a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), preserving the $e^{-itH}$ convention. Its [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\") decides how that gate is turned into rotations. Note that this is a *second*, independent product formula, acting on qubits after the mapping: Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) is passed here, and step 7 replaces it with one that knows about flow sets.\n"
msgstr "**Pemalam sintesis.** [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") menerima fungsi pemeta secara langsung, memetakan Hamiltonian gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") dengannya, dan mengeluarkan [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), sambil mengekalkan konvensyen $e^{-itH}$. [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\") menentukan bagaimana gate itu ditukar kepada putaran. Perhatikan bahawa ini ialah formula hasil darab *kedua* yang bebas, bertindak ke atas qubit selepas pemetaan: [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) Qiskit dihantar di sini, dan langkah 7 menggantikannya dengan yang mengetahui tentang set aliran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since every comparison below reruns this pipeline, it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Memandangkan setiap perbandingan di bawah menjalankan semula saluran paip ini, wajar ia dibungkus sekali sahaja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four fermionic modes have become a five-qubit circuit, with the ancilla supplied by the custom layout.\n"
msgstr "Empat mod fermion telah menjadi litar lima qubit, dengan ancilla dibekalkan oleh susun atur tersuai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now look at what the resulting circuit actually contains. Decomposing repeatedly reduces the evolution gates all the way down to `U` and `CX`, so that the two-qubit cost of the two synthesis strategies compared below is measured in the same currency: [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) then reports the `CX` count, and [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) takes a filter function to measure the two-qubit depth. Note that this `reps` is a decomposition depth, unrelated to the number of Trotter steps a product formula takes, which also goes by `reps` later in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang lihat apa yang sebenarnya terkandung dalam litar yang terhasil. Penguraian berulang mengurangkan gate evolusi sehingga ke `U` dan `CX`, supaya kos dua-qubit bagi dua strategi sintesis yang dibandingkan di bawah diukur dalam unit yang sama: [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) kemudian melaporkan bilangan `CX`, dan [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) menerima fungsi penapis untuk mengukur kedalaman dua-qubit. Perhatikan bahawa `reps` ini ialah kedalaman penguraian, tidak berkaitan dengan bilangan langkah Trotter yang diambil oleh formula hasil darab, yang juga dipanggil `reps` kemudian dalam panduan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twenty-six `CX` gates in twenty-three layers, so almost nothing runs in parallel. Drawing the circuit shows why:\n"
msgstr "Dua puluh enam gate `CX` dalam dua puluh tiga lapisan, jadi hampir tiada apa yang berjalan selari. Melukis litar menunjukkan sebabnya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every term has been compiled in isolation: a basis change, a `CX` ladder down to a single rotation, then the ladder is undone. The weight-1 flow set is free; its terms are lone rotations with no ladder around them, but each weight-3 term pays for four `CX`gates, and because the ladders are emitted sequentially, nothing overlaps.\n"
msgstr "Setiap sebutan telah dikompil secara terasing: penukaran asas, tangga `CX` sehingga satu putaran, kemudian tangga itu dibatalkan. Set aliran berat-1 percuma; sebutannya ialah putaran tunggal tanpa tangga di sekelilingnya, tetapi setiap sebutan berat-3 menanggung empat gate `CX`, dan kerana tangga dikeluarkan secara berjujukan, tiada apa yang bertindih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the grouping survives the whole pipeline (three flow sets, three mapped [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)s) and still buys almost nothing. The fermionic Trotterization of step 5 did its job; what wastes it is the *qubit-side* formula. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receives a set of terms it happens to be told nothing about, and compiles each in isolation. It cannot know they mutually commute, so it serializes what could share a basis change.\n"
msgstr "Jadi pengelompokan bertahan sepanjang saluran paip (tiga set aliran, tiga [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) yang dipetakan) namun masih hampir tidak memberi apa-apa faedah. Penghampiran Trotter fermion pada langkah 5 telah menjalankan tugasnya; yang membazirkannya ialah formula di *sebelah qubit*. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) menerima satu set sebutan yang kebetulan tidak diberitahu apa-apa tentangnya, dan mengkompil setiap satu secara terasing. Ia tidak dapat mengetahui bahawa semuanya saling kalis tukar tertib, jadi ia menyirikan apa yang boleh berkongsi satu penukaran asas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the gap this encoding exists to close: two product formulas are at work, and only the fermionic one has been given the structure so far. The next step supplies a qubit-side synthesis that exploits it too.\n"
msgstr "Itulah jurang yang wujud pengekodan ini untuk menutupnya: dua formula hasil darab sedang berfungsi, dan setakat ini hanya yang fermion telah diberi struktur itu. Langkah seterusnya membekalkan sintesis di sebelah qubit yang turut memanfaatkannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. A flow-set-aware synthesis {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "7. Sintesis yang peka set aliran {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recovering the advantage means telling the qubit-side synthesis about the structure. This is Section IV C of Ref. <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): because all terms of a flow set commute, they can be simultaneously diagonalized by a single Clifford circuit, rotated in one shared basis and rotated back, instead of once per term.\n"
msgstr "Memulihkan kelebihan bermakna memberitahu sintesis di sebelah qubit tentang struktur itu. Ini ialah Bahagian IV C Rujukan <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): kerana semua sebutan bagi satu set aliran saling kalis tukar tertib, ia boleh dipepenjurukan serentak oleh satu litar Clifford, diputar dalam satu asas bersama dan diputar kembali, dan bukannya sekali bagi setiap sebutan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this encoding, the Clifford is simple. Conjugating by a chain of `CZ` gates on nearest neighbors maps\n"
msgstr "Bagi pengekodan ini, Clifford itu mudah. Mengkonjugat dengan rantai gate `CZ` pada jiran terdekat memetakan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "simultaneously for every $j$. One `CZ` chain turns the entire weight-3 (west) flow set into a layer of independent single-qubit $X$ rotations. The [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) interface only requests a [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize) method, which is all this class implements. It carries no number of Trotter steps, because it receives one flow set at a time and so cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. That subdivision belongs a level up, in fermionic space, where an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") sees all of them at once (see [step 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"
msgstr "serentak untuk setiap $j$. Satu rantai `CZ` menukarkan keseluruhan set aliran berat-3 (barat) kepada satu lapisan putaran $X$ qubit tunggal yang bebas. Antara muka [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) hanya meminta kaedah [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize), dan itu sahaja yang dilaksanakan oleh kelas ini. Ia tidak membawa bilangan langkah Trotter, kerana ia menerima satu set aliran pada satu masa dan oleh itu tidak dapat membahagikan evolusi merentasi set-set itu. Pembahagian itu terletak satu peringkat di atas, dalam ruang fermion, tempat [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") melihat kesemuanya sekaligus (lihat [langkah 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Two details are easy to miss. A custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) must expose a `preserve_order` attribute, which the high-level-synthesis pass reads.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Dua perincian mudah terlepas pandang. [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) tersuai mesti mendedahkan atribut `preserve_order`, yang dibaca oleh pas sintesis aras tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Both helpers emit their gates in explicit layers rather than in term order, because [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) schedules gates *as soon as possible, in the order they were added*. Since all the gates within one of these sets commute, the order is free to choose. A term-by-term synthesis chooses the order badly. Emitting the overlapping `CZ` chain sequentially reports a depth that grows with the qubit count rather than the constant `2` the hardware could achieve.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kedua-dua pembantu mengeluarkan gate mereka dalam lapisan eksplisit dan bukan mengikut tertib sebutan, kerana [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) menjadualkan gate *secepat mungkin, mengikut tertib ia ditambah*. Memandangkan semua gate dalam satu set ini saling kalis tukar tertib, tertibnya bebas dipilih. Sintesis sebutan demi sebutan memilih tertib dengan buruk. Mengeluarkan rantai `CZ` yang bertindih secara berjujukan melaporkan kedalaman yang bertambah dengan bilangan qubit dan bukannya `2` malar yang dapat dicapai oleh perkakasan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Nota\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is why the synthesis above carries no number of Trotter steps. It receives one flow set per gate, so a repetition inside it would repeat *within* a set rather than cycling between them:\n"
msgstr "  Inilah sebabnya sintesis di atas tidak membawa bilangan langkah Trotter. Ia menerima satu set aliran bagi setiap gate, jadi pengulangan di dalamnya akan mengulang *dalam* satu set dan bukan berkitar antara set-set itu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The first form buys nothing: consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/2) A(t/2)` is just `A(t)` and the error stays at its one-step value however many steps are asked for.\n"
msgstr "  Bentuk pertama tidak memberi apa-apa faedah: eksponen berturut-turut bagi operator yang sama saling kalis tukar tertib, jadi `A(t/2) A(t/2)` hanyalah `A(t)` dan ralat kekal pada nilai satu langkahnya walau berapa banyak langkah diminta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The step count therefore belongs to the fermionic [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") of [step 5](#flowsets-build), which reads the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") and can interleave them. That division of labor is the point: the fermionic formula decides *how many steps* and *in what order*, and this class decides *how cheaply* each resulting set is realized.\n"
msgstr "  Oleh itu bilangan langkah tergolong pada [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") fermion dalam [langkah 5](#flowsets-build), yang membaca [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") dan boleh menyisipkannya. Pembahagian tugas itulah intinya: formula fermion memutuskan *berapa banyak langkah* dan *dalam tertib apa*, dan kelas ini memutuskan *betapa murahnya* setiap set yang terhasil direalisasikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To select the order, pass it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), which is the argument `flow_set_pass_manager` takes. Nothing else about the pipeline (or the fermionic circuit it runs on) changes:\n"
msgstr "Untuk memilih tertib, hantarkannya kepada [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), iaitu argumen yang diterima oleh `flow_set_pass_manager`. Tiada apa-apa lagi tentang saluran paip (atau litar fermion yang dijalankannya) berubah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From depth 23 with 26 `CX` gates down to depth 12 with 22 `CX` gates. Note that this is fewer entangling gates and nearly half the depth. Comparing the two pictures, the difference is not that the gates are cheaper but that they *stack*. The serial ladders are gone; entangling gates now sit above one another in shared layers because the whole west flow set is rotated in a single shared basis and the interaction is emitted in layers of disjoint pairs.\n"
msgstr "Daripada kedalaman 23 dengan 26 gate `CX` kepada kedalaman 12 dengan 22 gate `CX`. Perhatikan bahawa ini ialah gate berlilit yang lebih sedikit dan hampir separuh kedalaman. Membandingkan kedua-dua gambar, perbezaannya bukan kerana gate lebih murah tetapi kerana ia *bertindan*. Tangga bersiri telah hilang; gate berlilit kini berada di atas satu sama lain dalam lapisan bersama kerana keseluruhan set aliran barat diputar dalam satu asas bersama dan interaksi dikeluarkan dalam lapisan pasangan yang tidak bersentuhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` pattern-matches *absolute* qubit indices, which is safe here only because every flow set of this Hamiltonian spans the whole register. A fermionic product formula narrows each factor to the modes it actually touches, so a grouping whose sets covered only part of the chain would arrive relabeled and the patterns above would not match.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` memadankan corak indeks qubit *mutlak*, yang selamat di sini hanya kerana setiap set aliran Hamiltonian ini merentasi keseluruhan daftar. Formula hasil darab fermion mengecilkan setiap faktor kepada mod yang benar-benar disentuhnya, jadi pengelompokan yang set-setnya hanya meliputi sebahagian rantai akan tiba dengan label baharu dan corak di atas tidak akan sepadan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both drawings show the circuit after `decompose(reps=6)`, which rewrites everything into the `U` and `CX` basis, so the `CZ`, `Rx`, and `Rzz` gates emitted by `FlowSetSynthesis` are not visible as such. That is deliberate: it puts both circuits in the same basis, which is the only way the two-qubit counts and depths above are comparable. It is the *layer structure* that is notable in these figures, not the gate labels.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua-dua lukisan menunjukkan litar selepas `decompose(reps=6)`, yang menulis semula segala-galanya ke dalam asas `U` dan `CX`, jadi gate `CZ`, `Rx`, dan `Rzz` yang dikeluarkan oleh `FlowSetSynthesis` tidak kelihatan sebagai demikian. Ini disengajakan: ia meletakkan kedua-dua litar dalam asas yang sama, satu-satunya cara bilangan dan kedalaman dua-qubit di atas boleh dibandingkan. Yang ketara dalam rajah ini ialah *struktur lapisan*, bukan label gate.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"constant-depth-at-scale\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-scaling\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Constant depth at scale {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"
msgstr "8. Kedalaman malar pada skala besar {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interesting question is not the count at four modes but how it *scales*. The two `CZ` brickwork layers do not grow with the chain length, so the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step should be constant. Measuring it directly on the full Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian, well past what could be simulated by brute force:\n"
msgstr "Soalan yang menarik bukanlah bilangan pada empat mod tetapi bagaimana ia *berskala*. Dua lapisan batu-bata `CZ` tidak bertambah dengan panjang rantai, jadi kedalaman dua-qubit bagi satu langkah Trotter sepatutnya malar. Mengukurnya secara langsung pada Hamiltonian Fermi-Hubbard penuh, jauh melepasi apa yang boleh disimulasikan dengan daya kasar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit **depth stays at 12** from four modes to 100, while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) grows linearly to 407. The flow sets let it parallelize a little *within* the pipeline, but each set is still Trotterized term by term, so the growth is only slowed, not removed:\n"
msgstr "**Kedalaman** dua-qubit **kekal pada 12** dari empat mod hingga 100, manakala [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) bertambah secara linear kepada 407. Set aliran membolehkannya menyelari sedikit *dalam* saluran paip, tetapi setiap set masih dihampiri Trotter sebutan demi sebutan, jadi pertumbuhan itu hanya diperlahankan, bukan dihapuskan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gate count grows linearly under both (there are $O(N)$ terms to apply, and that is unavoidable), but the flow-set synthesis applies them in a constant number of parallel layers. This is the constant-depth result of Ref. <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"
msgstr "Bilangan gate bertambah secara linear di bawah kedua-duanya (terdapat $O(N)$ sebutan untuk dikenakan, dan itu tidak dapat dielakkan), tetapi sintesis set aliran mengenakannya dalam bilangan lapisan selari yang malar. Ini ialah keputusan kedalaman malar Rujukan <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The depth 12 splits across the three flow sets as 0 + 4 + 8, at every chain length. The east flow set contributes **zero**; it is bare `Rx` rotations. The west flow set costs 4, from the two `CZ` brickwork layers going in and the two coming out; dropping the interaction leaves a two-qubit depth of **four** at any chain length. The remaining **eight** is the interaction whose `Rzz` terms act on both nearest and next-nearest neighbors and so need four disjoint layers, each costing two `CX`gates. Four is optimal here: every interior qubit carries four `Rzz` gates (two to each neighbor and two to each next-nearest one) and can only take part in one at a time, so no schedule can do better.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedalaman 12 terbahagi merentasi tiga set aliran sebagai 0 + 4 + 8, pada setiap panjang rantai. Set aliran timur menyumbang **sifar**; ia hanyalah putaran `Rx` semata-mata. Set aliran barat berharga 4, daripada dua lapisan batu-bata `CZ` yang masuk dan dua yang keluar; menggugurkan interaksi meninggalkan kedalaman dua-qubit **empat** pada sebarang panjang rantai. Baki **lapan** ialah interaksi yang sebutan `Rzz`nya bertindak ke atas jiran terdekat dan jiran terdekat kedua, justeru memerlukan empat lapisan tidak bersentuhan, setiap satu berharga dua gate `CX`. Empat adalah optimum di sini: setiap qubit dalaman membawa empat gate `Rzz` (dua kepada setiap jiran dan dua kepada setiap jiran terdekat kedua) dan hanya boleh mengambil bahagian dalam satu pada satu masa, jadi tiada jadual yang boleh lebih baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Two thirds of the depth is the interaction, which shows that this encoding excels at the hopping, and thus at the dynamics of a free-fermion chain. However, note that the interaction does not commute with the hopping. Leaving it out is *not* an approximation to Fermi-Hubbard but a different model. Where the balance falls for a given problem is worth exploring.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dua pertiga daripada kedalaman ialah interaksi, yang menunjukkan bahawa pengekodan ini cemerlang pada lompatan, dan seterusnya pada dinamik rantai fermion bebas. Namun, perhatikan bahawa interaksi tidak kalis tukar tertib dengan lompatan. Mengabaikannya *bukan* penghampiran kepada Fermi-Hubbard tetapi model yang berbeza. Di mana keseimbangan terletak bagi sesuatu masalah wajar diterokai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"check-the-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-check-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Check the dynamics {#9-check-the-dynamics}"
msgstr "9. Semak dinamik {#9-check-the-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under the domain-wall map, an occupation pattern becomes a cumulative-parity string, so the initial state is prepared differently than under Jordan-Wigner. This is an easily overlooked practical consequence of delocalizing the parity. The helper from step 4 gives the right label:\n"
msgstr "Di bawah peta domain-wall, corak penghunian menjadi rentetan pariti kumulatif, jadi keadaan awal disediakan secara berbeza daripada di bawah Jordan-Wigner. Ini ialah akibat praktikal yang mudah terlepas pandang daripada penyahsetempatan pariti. Pembantu daripada langkah 4 memberikan label yang betul:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the state prepared, two questions remain, and they are best asked separately: does the flow-set synthesis compute the *right* thing, and does it compute it more *cheaply*?\n"
msgstr "Dengan keadaan telah disediakan, dua soalan kekal, dan yang terbaik ialah ditanya secara berasingan: adakah sintesis set aliran mengira perkara yang *betul*, dan adakah ia mengiranya dengan lebih *murah*?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Take correctness first. `FlowSetSynthesis` and Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receive the same encoded flow sets from the same fermionic Trotterization, so they must realize the same unitary up to a global phase. The custom Cliffords reorganize the work; they do not change the result. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Ambil ketepatan dahulu. `FlowSetSynthesis` dan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) Qiskit menerima set aliran terkod yang sama daripada penghampiran Trotter fermion yang sama, jadi mereka mesti merealisasikan uniter yang sama sehingga fasa global. Clifford tersuai menyusun semula kerja; ia tidak mengubah keputusan. Vektor keadaan rawak mengesan sebarang percanggahan dengan jauh lebih murah daripada membina uniter penuh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the *same* phase across several random states is what closes the gap. Checking more than one [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") matters too, since it confirms the agreement survives the interleaving of the flow sets rather than holding only for a single sweep.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua-dua bahagian semakan itu penting. Pertindihan modulus-unit pada satu keadaan adalah perlu tetapi tidak mencukupi: sintesis yang tersilap fasa bergantung keadaan masih akan menunjukkannya. Memerlukan fasa yang *sama* merentasi beberapa keadaan rawak ialah yang menutup jurang itu. Menyemak lebih daripada satu [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") juga penting, kerana ia mengesahkan persetujuan itu bertahan melalui penyisipan set aliran dan bukan hanya untuk satu sapuan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the choice of qubit-side synthesis is free of consequence for accuracy, which is what makes a cost comparison meaningful. The remaining question is what the encoding as a whole buys against the obvious alternative: plain Jordan-Wigner on `num_sites` qubits, with no ancilla and no custom Cliffords. Both the encoding and the qubit-side synthesis differ between the two columns, but the check above showed the latter cannot affect the result, so what the fidelities test is the encoding. Both pipelines also start from the *same* fermionic Trotterization, so any difference in fidelity would indicate a bug rather than a trade-off. The two columns are the *encodings*, flow-set against Jordan-Wigner:\n"
msgstr "Jadi pilihan sintesis di sebelah qubit tidak memberi kesan kepada ketepatan, dan itulah yang menjadikan perbandingan kos bermakna. Soalan yang tinggal ialah apa yang diperoleh pengekodan secara keseluruhan berbanding alternatif yang jelas: Jordan-Wigner biasa pada `num_sites` qubit, tanpa ancilla dan tanpa Clifford tersuai. Pengekodan dan sintesis di sebelah qubit kedua-duanya berbeza antara dua lajur, tetapi semakan di atas menunjukkan yang kemudian tidak boleh menjejaskan keputusan, jadi apa yang diuji oleh kesetiaan ialah pengekodan. Kedua-dua saluran paip juga bermula daripada penghampiran Trotter fermion yang *sama*, jadi sebarang perbezaan dalam kesetiaan akan menunjukkan pepijat dan bukan pertukaran. Kedua-dua lajur ialah *pengekodan*, set aliran berbanding Jordan-Wigner:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the fidelity column first: identical, to every printed digit, in two different Hilbert spaces under two different encodings. That is the fermionic Trotterization showing through. The approximation was fixed in step 5, before either encoding was chosen, so both circuits carry exactly the error of a first-order formula over three flow sets, and it falls roughly four-fold per doubling of the step count.\n"
msgstr "Baca lajur kesetiaan dahulu: serupa, sehingga setiap digit yang dicetak, dalam dua ruang Hilbert yang berbeza di bawah dua pengekodan yang berbeza. Itulah penghampiran Trotter fermion yang kelihatan. Penghampiran telah ditetapkan pada langkah 5, sebelum mana-mana pengekodan dipilih, jadi kedua-dua litar membawa ralat formula peringkat pertama yang sama tepat merentasi tiga set aliran, dan ia jatuh kira-kira empat kali ganda bagi setiap penggandaan bilangan langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the encodings do differ in is cost, and the trade is worth stating plainly. The flow set spends **more** entangling gates: 22 against 18 at one step. The ancilla is not the reason, since it carries no two-qubit gate of its own. The reason is the interaction, exactly as [step 3](#flowsets-encoding) warned: delocalizing the parity turns three nearest-neighbor `ZZ` terms into seven spanning nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors, and each costs two `CX` gates. That is the price paid for making the hopping cheap.\n"
msgstr "Apa yang berbeza antara pengekodan ialah kos, dan pertukaran itu wajar dinyatakan dengan jelas. Set aliran membelanjakan gate berlilit **lebih banyak**: 22 berbanding 18 pada satu langkah. Ancilla bukan puncanya, kerana ia tidak membawa gate dua-qubit sendiri. Puncanya ialah interaksi, tepat seperti yang diperingatkan oleh [langkah 3](#flowsets-encoding): penyahsetempatan pariti menukarkan tiga sebutan `ZZ` jiran terdekat kepada tujuh yang merentasi jiran terdekat *dan* jiran terdekat kedua, dan setiap satu berharga dua gate `CX`. Itulah harga yang dibayar untuk menjadikan lompatan murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It also wins only narrowly on depth at this size (12 against 14), because four modes is too small for the asymptotics to show. The point is the *scaling* measured in [step 8](#flowsets-scaling): that depth of 12 is constant, while the Jordan-Wigner depth grows with the chain. At 14 modes it is already 12 against 34.\n"
msgstr "Ia juga menang hanya tipis pada kedalaman pada saiz ini (12 berbanding 14), kerana empat mod terlalu kecil untuk asimptot kelihatan. Intinya ialah *penskalaan* yang diukur dalam [langkah 8](#flowsets-scaling): kedalaman 12 itu malar, manakala kedalaman Jordan-Wigner bertambah dengan rantai. Pada 14 mod ia sudah 12 berbanding 34.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) calls above are essential, for two independent reasons.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Amaran\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Panggilan [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) di atas adalah penting, atas dua sebab yang bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) and [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) use a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s *exact* definition, bypassing a custom qubit-side synthesis. Verifying against an un-decomposed circuit reports perfect fidelity even for a deliberately wrong synthesis.\n"
msgstr "  [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) dan [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) menggunakan takrifan *tepat* [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), memintas sintesis tersuai di sebelah qubit. Mengesahkan terhadap litar yang tidak diuraikan melaporkan kesetiaan sempurna walaupun bagi sintesis yang sengaja disalahkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The same applies one level up, to the fermionic synthesis. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed goes to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which maps it without consulting `Evolution.synthesis` at all, so [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") would silently have no effect. `trotter_steps` from step 5 performs that decomposition; a pipeline that sets the method with [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") gets the same expansion from the pass instead.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Perkara yang sama terpakai satu peringkat di atas, kepada sintesis fermion. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang tidak pernah diuraikan pergi ke peringkat fermion-ke-qubit secara keseluruhan, yang memetakannya tanpa merujuk `Evolution.synthesis` sama sekali, jadi [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") secara senyap tidak akan mempunyai kesan. `trotter_steps` daripada langkah 5 melaksanakan penguraian itu; saluran paip yang menetapkan kaedah dengan [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") mendapat pengembangan yang sama daripada pas itu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a final cross-check, the site densities $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ computed in the encoded space must reproduce the Jordan-Wigner result. This check is about the *encoding*, not the circuit, so no Trotter approximation enters it. Both time evolutions are computed exactly, by matrix exponentiation of the respective Hamiltonians. Any discrepancy would therefore point at the encoding rather than a product formula:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai semakan silang akhir, ketumpatan tapak $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ yang dikira dalam ruang terkod mesti menghasilkan semula keputusan Jordan-Wigner. Semakan ini mengenai *pengekodan*, bukan litar, jadi tiada penghampiran Trotter terlibat. Kedua-dua evolusi masa dikira dengan tepat, melalui eksponen matriks bagi Hamiltonian masing-masing. Oleh itu sebarang percanggahan akan menunjuk kepada pengekodan dan bukan formula hasil darab:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The densities agree to ten decimal places.\n"
msgstr "Ketumpatan bersetuju sehingga sepuluh tempat perpuluhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Apa yang perlu diingat {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping.** Flow sets are defined on the directed fermionic interaction graph, so the grouping is chosen while problem structure is still available. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute carries it into the circuit, where a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) turns it into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per flow set.\n"
msgstr "**Kelompokkan sebelum memetakan.** Set aliran ditakrifkan pada graf interaksi fermion berarah, jadi pengelompokan dipilih semasa struktur masalah masih tersedia. Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") membawanya ke dalam litar, di mana satu [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) menukarkannya kepada satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") bagi setiap set aliran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ancillas buy structure.** Spending one extra qubit turns an entire flow set into weight-1 Paulis, whose evolution needs no entangling gates. Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) observes this trade-off generally. Larger qubit-to-fermion ratios admit shallower evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Ancilla membeli struktur.** Membelanjakan satu qubit tambahan menukarkan keseluruhan set aliran kepada Pauli berat-1, yang evolusinya tidak memerlukan gate berlilit. Rujukan <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) memerhatikan pertukaran ini secara umum. Nisbah qubit-kepada-fermion yang lebih besar membolehkan litar evolusi yang lebih cetek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A custom encoding is one function.** Map a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") do the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Pengekodan tersuai ialah satu fungsi.** Petakan satu operator pindahan teritlak kepada rentetan Pauli; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") melakukan selebihnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The mapping and the grouping alone are not enough.** Splitting the evolution per flow set only slowed the linear growth in depth; a term-by-term synthesis of each set still threw away the fact that its terms commute. Only supplying a flow-set-aware [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) made the depth constant. Custom encodings, grouping, and custom synthesis are complementary: all three are needed.\n"
msgstr "**Pemetaan dan pengelompokan sahaja tidak mencukupi.** Memecahkan evolusi bagi setiap set aliran hanya memperlahankan pertumbuhan linear dalam kedalaman; sintesis sebutan demi sebutan bagi setiap set masih mengabaikan hakikat bahawa sebutannya saling kalis tukar tertib. Hanya membekalkan [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) yang peka set aliran menjadikan kedalaman malar. Pengekodan tersuai, pengelompokan, dan sintesis tersuai saling melengkapi: ketiga-tiganya diperlukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two product formulas, two jobs.** [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") fixes the approximation in fermionic space, where the grouping is still visible, so it alone sets the Trotter error and the step count. The qubit-side [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) then decides only how cheaply each set is realized: step 9 confirms both choices give the same unitary. Separating the two is what lets the accuracy and the cost be tuned independently. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"
msgstr "**Dua formula hasil darab, dua tugas.** [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") menetapkan penghampiran dalam ruang fermion, tempat pengelompokan masih kelihatan, jadi ia sahaja menentukan ralat Trotter dan bilangan langkah. [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) di sebelah qubit kemudian hanya memutuskan betapa murahnya setiap set direalisasikan: langkah 9 mengesahkan kedua-dua pilihan memberikan uniter yang sama. Memisahkan kedua-duanya membolehkan ketepatan dan kos ditala secara bebas. Lihat [Sintesiskan gate Evolution dalam ruang fermion](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify it.** An encoding that satisfies the commutation relations might still represent a different Hamiltonian if a prefactor or sign is off. Checking an intertwining relation (or, more cheaply, the spectrum) catches this.\n"
msgstr "**Sahkannya.** Pengekodan yang memenuhi hubungan komutasi mungkin masih mewakili Hamiltonian yang berbeza jika pemfaktor atau tanda tersilap. Menyemak hubungan penjalinan (atau, lebih murah, spektrum) mengesan perkara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `FlowSetSynthesis` above is deliberately written for *this* encoding on a 1D chain. It pattern-matches the specific Pauli labels the encoding produces and raises on anything else, rather than silently falling back to a generic product formula. A general implementation has two halves. Reading the flow-set structure from the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") is what a [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") for an evolution already does. Deriving the diagonalizing Clifford from the stabilizer group, as described in Section IV C of Ref.   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), is the half that remains encoding specific.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` di atas sengaja ditulis untuk pengekodan *ini* pada rantai 1D. Ia memadankan corak label Pauli khusus yang dihasilkan oleh pengekodan dan membangkitkan ralat pada apa-apa yang lain, dan bukan secara senyap kembali kepada formula hasil darab generik. Pelaksanaan umum mempunyai dua bahagian. Membaca struktur set aliran daripada [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") operator ialah apa yang sudah dilakukan oleh [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") bagi sesuatu evolusi. Menerbitkan Clifford pepenjuru daripada kumpulan penstabil, seperti yang diterangkan dalam Bahagian IV C Rujukan   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), ialah bahagian yang kekal khusus pengekodan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Also, delocalizing the parity makes the interaction term $n_j n_{j+1}$ weight-2 rather than diagonal in single qubits, which is the counterpart cost to the cheaper hopping terms.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Selain itu, penyahsetempatan pariti menjadikan sebutan interaksi $n_j n_{j+1}$ berat-2 dan bukan pepenjuru dalam qubit tunggal, yang merupakan kos sepadan kepada sebutan lompatan yang lebih murah.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next: two dimensions {#next-two-dimensions}"
msgstr "Seterusnya: dua dimensi {#next-two-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything above is one-dimensional, and deliberately so. On a chain, the flow sets are just the two arrow orientations, and the encoding needs a single ancilla. Neither simplification survives in two dimensions, which is where local encodings are needed.\n"
msgstr "Semua di atas adalah satu dimensi, dan sengaja begitu. Pada rantai, set aliran hanyalah dua orientasi anak panah, dan pengekodan memerlukan satu ancilla. Kedua-dua penyederhanaan ini tidak bertahan dalam dua dimensi, di mana pengekodan setempat diperlukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a planar lattice, a flow set is a directed path (or a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths) through the interaction graph, and finding a small set of such paths that covers every edge becomes a combinatorial problem in its own right, rather than a two-line classification. The encodings also change character; instead of a single ancilla for the whole chain, they add one per lattice site or cell. Verstraete-Cirac pairs every fermionic site with its own auxiliary qubit, a qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$, while Derby-Klassen places one at the center of each odd plaquette, for a ratio of $3/2$. The register layout then has genuine two-dimensional structure, and the stabilizer group that must be projected onto is no longer trivial. The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a *subspace*, which changes both state preparation and the verification recipe from [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
msgstr "Pada kekisi satah, set aliran ialah laluan berarah (atau kesatuan laluan berarah yang tidak bersentuhan bucu) melalui graf interaksi, dan mencari set kecil laluan sedemikian yang meliputi setiap tepi menjadi masalah kombinatorik tersendiri, dan bukan pengelasan dua baris. Pengekodan juga berubah sifat; dan bukannya satu ancilla bagi seluruh rantai, ia menambah satu bagi setiap tapak atau sel kekisi. Verstraete-Cirac memasangkan setiap tapak fermion dengan qubit tambahannya sendiri, nisbah qubit-kepada-mod $2$, manakala Derby-Klassen meletakkan satu di tengah setiap plakuet ganjil, bagi nisbah $3/2$. Susun atur daftar kemudian mempunyai struktur dua dimensi sebenar, dan kumpulan penstabil yang mesti diunjurkan padanya tidak lagi remeh. Hamiltonian terkod hanya setia pada *subruang*, yang mengubah kedua-dua penyediaan keadaan dan resipi pengesahan daripada [langkah 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pieces this guide builds are the ones that carry over: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for a register whose size differs from the mode count, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding itself, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") for wiring it into the transpiler, and a custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) for making the flow-set structure pay off. Only the encoding and the flow-set decomposition are different.\n"
msgstr "Komponen yang dibina oleh panduan ini ialah yang terbawa ke hadapan: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") untuk daftar yang saiznya berbeza daripada bilangan mod, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") untuk pengekodan itu sendiri, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") untuk menyambungkannya ke dalam transpiler, dan [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) tersuai untuk menjadikan struktur set aliran berbaloi. Hanya pengekodan dan penguraian set aliran yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [2D flow-set guide](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) picks up here, working through the Verstraete-Cirac encoding on a square lattice: four flow sets, a depth-2 Clifford for each, and the stabilizer projection the verification then needs.\n"
msgstr "[Panduan set aliran 2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) bersambung di sini, menyelesaikan pengekodan Verstraete-Cirac pada kekisi petak: empat set aliran, Clifford kedalaman-2 bagi setiap satu, dan unjuran penstabil yang kemudiannya diperlukan oleh pengesahan.\n"

